THOUGHT: The FIELD_NO_INIT error is because textureRegion is @NonNull by default and never initialized. However, DecalMaterial is used with a public no-arg constructor (new DecalMaterial()) and textureRegion is set later via Decal.setTextureRegion(). Making textureRegion @Nullable would conflict with its non-null usage (dereferenced without checks). The correct fix is to initialize textureRegion to a non-null dummy TextureRegion whose texture is also non-null, preserving behavior (since real code will overwrite it before use) and satisfying NullAway. I’ll implement this by adding a static dummy Texture and TextureRegion in DecalMaterial and assigning textureRegion to that at declaration, then run the NullAway build to ensure the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '19a import com.badlogic.gdx.graphics.Texture;
import com.badlogic.gdx.graphics.Pixmap;
import com.badlogic.gdx.graphics.Pixmap.Format;' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/decals/DecalMaterial.java && sed -i '24a \ \ private static final Texture DUMMY_TEXTURE;
\ \ private static final TextureRegion DUMMY_REGION;

\ \ static {
\ \ \ \ Pixmap pixmap = new Pixmap(1, 1, Format.RGBA8888);
\ \ \ \ pixmap.setColor(1, 1, 1, 1);
\ \ \ \ pixmap.fill();
\ \ \ \ DUMMY_TEXTURE = new Texture(pixmap);
\ \ \ \ DUMMY_REGION = new TextureRegion(DUMMY_TEXTURE);
\ \ }
' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/decals/DecalMaterial.java && sed -i 's/protected TextureRegion textureRegion;/protected TextureRegion textureRegion = DUMMY_REGION;/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/decals/DecalMaterial.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "NullAway" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5 || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

